    "recap": "Before 17,331 at STAPLES Center, Los Angeles broke a scoreless tie with three goals in just over six minutes of the second period. Kevin Dallman scored at 6:52, Anže Kopitar made it 2–0 at 9:14, and Dustin Brown converted a power play at 13:03. Rob Blake added the fourth at 11:54 of the third. Kopitar finished with a goal and two assists, while Erik Ersberg turned aside all 38 Phoenix shots for his second shutout of the season. Despite being outshot 38–33, the Kings earned a 4–0 victory in the first NHL game witnessed in Courtside Archive.",
